    55	revision, plus:
    56
    57	| Lens | Additional context |
    58	| --- | --- |
    59	| Evidence | sources, optional firsthand evidence, claim ledger |
    60	| Story | outline |
    61	| Clarity | extracted audience and constraints |
    62	| Copy | optional repository style guide |
    63
    64	Each owns `reviews/article-00N/<lens>/result.json` and `report.md`. The report
    65	must contain the same findings as JSON. The process's filesystem contains only
    66	the listed inputs under `context/` and its output root; it cannot browse the
    67	durable run or another review. This implementation omits prior-lens
    68	conversation and reports from reviewer assignments; a reviewer process has no
    69	inherited conversation from another lens.
     1	# Artifacts
     2
     3	## Run layout
     4
     5	```text
     6	<run-dir>/
     7	├── brief.md
     8	├── workflow.json
     9	├── evidence/
    10	│   ├── sources.md
    11	│   ├── firsthand.md                 # optional
    12	│   └── assets/
    13	├── claim-ledger.md
    14	├── outline.md
    15	├── drafts/
    16	│   ├── article-001.md
    17	│   └── article-00N.md
    18	├── reviews/
    19	│   └── article-00N/
    20	│       ├── evidence/{result.json,report.md}
    21	│       ├── story/{result.json,report.md}
    22	│       ├── clarity/{result.json,report.md}
    23	│       └── copy/{result.json,report.md}
    24	├── pm-decisions/
    25	│   └── article-00N.md
    26	├── article.md                        # success only
    27	└── .control/                         # post-cleanup audit copies
    28	```
    29
    30	Earlier candidates, partial lens sequences, reviews, and PM decisions are kept
    31	when a revision occurs or a run blocks. `article.md` is written only after all
    32	four final-candidate lenses pass PM routing and is byte-for-byte identical to
    33	that candidate.
    34
    35	## Review result
    36
    37	`result.json` has this validated minimum shape:
    38
    39	```json
    40	{
    41	  "status": "fix_required",
    42	  "lens": "clarity",
    43	  "reviewed_revision": "sha256:...",
    44	  "findings": [
    45	    {
    46	      "id": "clarity-001",
    47	      "severity": "must_fix",
    48	      "location": "section: Introduction",
    49	      "problem": "The requested action is not visible.",
    50	      "suggested_direction": "State the action before the background."
    51	    }
    52	  ]
    53	}
    54	```
    55
    56	Allowed statuses are `clean`, `fix_required`, and `blocked`. A clean result has
    57	no findings; `fix_required` has at least one. IDs are non-empty and unique
    58	within the result, all finding fields are non-empty, lens/revision must match
    59	the assignment, and `report.md` repeats every finding field.
    60
    61	## PM decision
    62
    63	`pm-decisions/article-00N.md` contains one fenced JSON object. Its `lenses` map
    64	accumulates only the lenses reached for that candidate:
    65
    66	```json
    67	{
    68	  "reviewed_revision": "sha256:...",
    69	  "lenses": {
    70	    "evidence": {
    71	      "request_id": "request-token",
    72	      "review_digest": "sha256:...",
    73	      "decisions": []
    74	    },
    75	    "story": {
    76	      "request_id": "request-token",
    77	      "review_digest": "sha256:...",
    78	      "decisions": [
    79	        {
    80	          "finding_id": "story-001",
    81	          "decision": "invalid",
    82	          "reason": "The candidate already satisfies the outline."
    83	        }
    84	      ]
    85	    }
    86	  }
    87	}
    88	```
    89
    90	Each reached lens covers every finding exactly once. Unknown, duplicate, or
    91	missing IDs, stale revisions, mismatched request IDs or review digests, dropped
    92	prior lenses, and prepopulated future lenses fail the contract.
    93
    94	## workflow.json
    95
    96	`workflow.json` is atomically rewritten and is the controller's source of
    97	truth. Schema version 1 records:
    98
    99	- `status`: `running`, `succeeded`, or `blocked`;
   100	- `phase`: current controller phase;
   101	- `current_candidate` and `current_revision` (`sha256:<hex>`);
   102	- `active_role`;
   103	- stable relative `artifact_paths`;
   104	- `review_attempt_count` (one per reviewer process);
   105	- `started_at`, `updated_at`, and terminal `completed_at` timestamps;
   106	- terminal `block_reason` when blocked.
   107
   108	The durable `.control/` directory is controller-owned and preserves audit
   109	copies of generated prompt assignments, per-invocation logs, and natural exit
   110	markers. Live launchers, PM requests, and agent workspaces exist only in
   111	controller-private temporary directories outside the durable run; they are
   112	removed after verified process cleanup and are never copied into `.control/`.
   113	Controller artifact access rejects symlink path components and non-regular
   114	files. Editorial completion never depends on tmux scrollback or chat
   115	transcripts.

